    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The full suite (the `acceptance` package is the only test module in this repo) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner soft-delete across the stack:\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added a `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`) defaulting to `Boolean.FALSE`, with getter/setter, so a newly created owner is `deleted = false`.\n- Added a static `isDeleted(Boolean)` helper (treats `null` as not-deleted) as the single definition of the deleted check.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `deleteOwner` now marks the owner deleted and saves it (`owner.setDeleted(true); clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`) instead of removing the row, still returning `204 No Content` (2xx). The row is retained and remains readable via GET.\n- `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (the normally-blocking hard/household duplicate check) and `findPossibleDuplicate` (soft-duplicate identity check) now filter out soft-deleted owners, so a duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been deleted.\n\n**API schema** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema so `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it into GET responses.\n\n**DB schema** (hsqldb / h2 / mysql / postgres `schema.sql`)\n- Added the `deleted` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (GET shows `deleted:false`, then `true` after DELETE) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (recreating a deleted owner is allowed) \u2014 both pass, and the full build is green.",
